Subject: [PATCH] basu: port the sd-bus compatibility seams to Darwin

Darwin exposes the BSD local-socket credential APIs used by basu's
FreeBSD path. Use those paths on Apple targets and map endian operations
to libkern's OSByteOrder API. Darwin has no ELF start/stop section symbols,
so retain and search the built-in error table directly.

diff -ruN a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build	2022-12-16 02:13:02
+++ b/meson.build	2026-07-29 18:36:00
@@ -265,7 +265,9 @@
 subdir('src/basic')
 subdir('src/libsystemd')
 subdir('src/systemd')
+if host_machine.system() != 'darwin'
 subdir('src/test')
+endif
 
 foreach tuple : tests
         sources = tuple[0]
